The license is MIT and stands alone in LICENSE. This file says what came
from where.

Every effect is generated from Airwindows by Chris Johnson
(https://github.com/airwindows/airwindows), used under the MIT License in
third_party/airwindows/LICENSE (Copyright (c) 2018 Chris Johnson).
tools/awgen reads each plug-in's upstream source and writes
src/airwindows/plugins/<Name>.c, a C translation of its processing loop,
constructor and parameters; third_party/airwindows/ORIGIN.txt names the
upstream commit and what was changed.

Upstream's source is not included. The generator and the reference tests
read a checkout of it at that commit (.cache/airwindows-upstream); the
tests compile it to check each generated kernel against it, and nothing in
the package is built from it.

The nodes run on audiodsp (https://github.com/PyDevices/audiodsp, MIT),
which this package depends on and does not include.
